{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_dispatcher", "label": "Dispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decides when the runtime pulls the next envelope and runs onReceive; the choice between the microtask and macrotask queues drives throughput, fairness and latency."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_hybriddispatcher", "label": "HybridDispatcher (default)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "setImmediate costs ~2.4 us, which a flooded actor amortises and a one-request-at-a-time actor cannot \u2014 measured 8.1 us per round trip on a 10 000-exchange volley, roughly 4.8 us of it scheduling. queueMicrotask is ~4x faster but unusable alone because microtasks drain before timers or I/O. The hybrid takes the speed and bounds the unfairness; its worst case is exactly what ImmediateDispatcher always did."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_microtaskdispatcher", "label": "MicrotaskDispatcher", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A measurement tool, not a production choice: no escape at all, so any workload that keeps actors busy starves timers, sockets and HTTP responses while the process looks healthy."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_immediatedispatcher", "label": "ImmediateDispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_throughputdispatcher", "label": "ThroughputDispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only dispatcher holding a scheduling queue of its own, drained from the front throughput times per tick \u2014 a RingBuffer for the same reason a mailbox is."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_hybrid_budget", "label": "64-unit microtask budget", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The count lives on the dispatcher rather than on each actor: the microtask chain is the union across every actor scheduled on it, so a per-actor budget would read 1 for each of two actors volleying forever \u2014 undercounting in precisely the case the budget exists to bound."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_dispatcher_interface", "label": "Dispatcher interface (id / execute / onError)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_dispatchererror", "label": "DispatcherError", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fires for faults supervision structurally cannot see, so the channel is quiet by design \u2014 traffic on it means something is wrong underneath your actors; treat one as a page, not a counter. Caught at the actor cell, so it works for third-party dispatchers the system never sees."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_per_actor_dispatcher", "label": "Per-actor dispatcher via ActorOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_throughput_knobs", "label": "Two different throughput knobs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A dispatcher throughput counts queued turns, one per actor; how many messages one actor handles in its turn is ActorOptions.withThroughput or actor-ts.actor.throughput."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_sync_dispatcher_antipattern", "label": "Synchronous dispatcher anti-pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Synchronous execution defeats actor-model invariants \u2014 tell stops being fire-and-forget and the receiver await stalls the caller stack."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_tracing_dispatcher", "label": "Wrap-and-delegate custom dispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_dispatcher", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_dispatchers_hybriddispatcher", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/dispatchers.mdx", "source_loc